# Go sources are stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks out CRLF while gofmt
# writes LF, so every formatted file looks modified and line endings leak
# into diffs. Pinning eol here removes that whole class of churn.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Schema migrations are HASHED, so their bytes are part of the contract.
#
# db/schema.go embeds migrations/*.sql and records sha256(file) in certen_schema_history; Verify then
# re-hashes the embedded bytes and compares. A CRLF checkout therefore produces a binary whose baseline
# hash differs from the one a Linux-built binary wrote, and that binary REFUSES to start against a
# perfectly good production database — reporting "checksum mismatch", which reads like corruption.
#
# Observed 2026-09-18 while recovering a fleet outage: a Windows-built recovery tool computed
# a6d06c0b… for 00000_baseline.sql where production held dacf9261…, the LF hash of the same file.
db/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
db/*.fingerprint text eol=lf

# The deployed ZK verification key is embedded by its exact bytes (pkg/crypto/bls_zkp/verifier_v2.go pins its SHA-256).
pkg/crypto/bls_zkp/*.bin binary

# The sigtypes conformance vectors are HASHED (manifest.json pins every file's sha256) and are copied byte-for-byte into the
# TypeScript verifier's repo. A CRLF checkout would make the pinned hashes fail on Windows and the copies differ.
accumulate-lite-client-2/liteclient/proof/govsig/testdata/sigtypes/*.json text eol=lf
# A golden is specification: its bytes are never normalised.
accumulate-lite-client-2/liteclient/proof/consolidated_governance-proof/testdata/*.golden.json text eol=lf

# The finality pins file is HASHED as raw bytes (pkg/finality PINS_SHA256) and mirrored byte-identically into the other
# repos, and the finality vectors, states registry and manifest are copied byte-for-byte into the TypeScript verifier's repo.
# A CRLF checkout would make the pinned hashes fail on Windows.
pkg/finality/pins/*.json text eol=lf
pkg/finality/testdata/finality/*.json text eol=lf
pkg/finality/testdata/finality_chain1/* text eol=lf
pkg/finality/testdata/finality_chain2/* text eol=lf

# finality_eth_sepolia1 (RB11-C2): every file is hashed in its MANIFEST and copied byte-for-byte into the TypeScript repository; the link files are hashed by link_sha256.
pkg/finality/ethsepolia/testdata/finality_eth_sepolia1/** -text
pkg/finality/pins-links/* -text

# RB11-INT3 (C2 finding F5): every published finality vector set directory carries a rule that keeps its bytes (adiri, arbfinal and
# ethl1 through their testdata/.gitattributes; arb_posted1, base_posted1 and base_final1 through their own; chain1, chain2 and the
# registry/pins snapshots above; eth_sepolia1 and pins-links above). The loose files directly under pkg/finality/testdata are
# specification too (the addendum golden, the pinned go.mod requirement list, SUPERSEDED.md, the mutation-equivalents lists and the
# golden generator): a CRLF checkout must not rewrite them.
pkg/finality/testdata/* -text
pkg/finality/testdata/finality/*.txt -text
# RB11-E2E-POS: the recorded Settlements of the published vectors' leg blocks are hashed in their MANIFEST.json; a CRLF checkout must not rewrite them.
cmd/proofverify/testdata/finality_e2e_pos1/* -text
pkg/finality/ethsepolia/testdata/finality_eth_sepolia2/** -text
pkg/finality/ethsepolia/testdata/finality_eth_sepolia3/** -text

# The validator image is built on a Linux host from a git checkout, and the shell scripts that build and deploy it run
# there under /bin/sh. A CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) puts a carriage return at the end of every line:
# `sh deploy/make-base-images.sh` then stops on its first `set` line, and a Dockerfile RUN line carries a stray CR into
# its command. The base-image Dockerfiles and the script that resolves and records their package versions are part of the
# reproducible-build claim (docs/l4/REPRODUCIBLE_BUILD.md), so their bytes are LF everywhere.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
deploy/base-images/Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
deploy/*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/base-images/*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/base-images.lock text eol=lf
